experiments/002-living-map/golden-valley/models.json:2:  "note": "Which type models this copy of the map has. Both Meshy GLBs are PARKED as of task 001 part 2 (10 Sep): image-to-3D gave soft, blobby architecture and turned every pane of glass into holes, so the campus block and the NCIC are built from rules in facades.js instead \u2014 exact on every footprint, crisp at any distance, and about ninety lines of GLSL against 11.32 MB of GLB. The files stay in meshy/ rather than being deleted; this list is how the map is told not to ask for them. scripts/build_site.py rewrites this file for a public build.",
experiments/002-living-map/generate/cheltenham-circular-footpath/out/codex-prompts.md:7:Use case: sketch-to-render. Edit target: the supplied surveyed 3D render a-start.png. Produce one photorealistic photograph at 1280x720, exact same camera 14 m above ground, framing and projected geometry. This is a material and sky replacement, not landscape redesign. Keep all object boundaries and positions. Horizon ground at y=330 of 720, housing/tree silhouette as input. Preserve path centerline from approximately (650,720) via (746,581) to (479,340); preserve its bend, widths and perspective. Preserve brook centerline from (1280,484) via (1050,440),(800,391),(577,360),(607,351). Preserve all tractor working lines and single far-left hedge. Keep agricultural shed exact bottom-left silhouette, flat weathered roof corners around (0,503),(466,459),(551,484), wall ending (552,543); no roof pitch change. Keep housing and tree edge at exact original positions; render houses red brick with grey slate and red clay roofs, mature full-leaf trees. GCHQ is the low broad building on right horizon (roughly x=920–1180,y=306–333), retain its silhouette and render pale white-grey metal roofing, NEVER water. Real late summer English pasture with fine grass texture, trodden bare-earth/flattened-grass path, subtle real tractor lines. Small brook with restrained rushes along existing banks, do not widen or relocate it. Warm afternoon sunlight from upper left, blue sky with a few small white cumulus, clear distant visibility. Natural photographic textures and exposure, low drone photograph, no CGI look. Drop sky specks or retain only a few tiny distant rooks no larger than original. No people, vehicles, text, glowing lines, new hedges or new features. Exact surveyed layout takes priority over prettification.
experiments/002-living-map/generate/cheltenham-circular-footpath/out/codex-prompts.md:8:CORRECTION PASS: First reference is the authoritative original geometry; second is only the desired photographic material/light reference. Correct drift from second: brook became wider and its small bends changed; housing/tree silhouettes changed; tractor lines changed; foreground path bend slightly rounded. Trace those features exactly from FIRST reference. Do not alter horizon height. Keep original shed footprint, and original grey yard/ground region behind shed instead of replacing it with pasture. Preserve the original brook as a very thin line with modest rushes, not a broad drainage ditch. Preserve exact existing housing roof positions and heights while changing only materials. Keep matching photographic warmth and season of second image.
experiments/002-living-map/generate/cheltenham-circular-footpath/out/codex-prompts.md:12:Use case: sketch-to-render. First reference b-end.png is the EDIT TARGET and authoritative surveyed geometry. Second reference is ONLY a photographic lighting/material/season reference, never copy its layout. Make one photorealistic low drone photograph, exact camera 14m above ground and exact framing of FIRST reference, 16:9. Change placeholder materials and sky only. Preserve ground horizon at y=272/720 at left and exact housing/tree silhouette. Preserve footpath straight up middle from x=640 at bottom to x=641,y=290, exact width/perspective. Preserve the narrow stream on right with exact line and loop near (720,300), continuing via (860,325),(1060,355) to (1280,401); small real brook, thin modest rush margins, do not widen or move. Preserve all original field tractor working lines exactly. Preserve housing footprints and roof/tree positions along horizon, change houses to red brick with grey slate and red clay tile roofs, mature trees in full leaf. Real late summer English pasture, fine green and straw grass matching second reference, path bare earth and flattened grass, real subtle tractor lines. Same warm afternoon sun from upper left, blue sky with a few cumulus, clear air to horizon; taken minutes after second reference 320m farther along route. Natural photographic texture and exposure matching second reference. A few tiny distant rooks permitted, never enlarge original sky specks. No people, vehicles, text, glowing lines, new hedges, sheds or buildings. Exact FIRST image layout is mandatory; no camera tilt, zoom, reframing or landscape redesign.
experiments/002-living-map/generate/cheltenham-circular-footpath/out/codex-prompts.md:19:A initial: broad path alignment and horizon preserved; brook widened and small bends changed; housing/tree silhouettes and tractor lines reinterpreted. Yard behind shed became grass.
experiments/002-living-map/generate/cheltenham-circular-footpath/out/codex-prompts.md:21:A final: brook narrowed after correction. Horizon approximately retained; path broadly aligned but bend rounded and widths changed. Brook small bends and bank widths still differ. Housing and tree silhouettes are not exact. Far-left hedge is slightly shorter. Tractor lines are altered/subdued. Shed footprint broadly retained, but roof boundary/detail and ground behind it changed; grey yard behind shed remains pasture. GCHQ stays a pale metal-roofed building at right, with altered architectural detail.
experiments/002-living-map/generate/cheltenham-circular-footpath/out/codex-prompts.md:25:B final: horizon still approximately 18 pixels too high (left ground line about y=254 versus input y=272). Housing edge remains lifted and individual roof/tree silhouettes differ. Distant path shifts about 15 pixels left (x≈626 versus x≈641); foreground remains near centre, width changes. Brook right-edge crossing is close (about y=398 versus y=401), but middle segment/loop is higher and reshaped; banks wider. Tractor lines differ.
