experiments/002-living-map/meshy/src/codex-notes.md:21:Use case: product-mockup. Generate A1, one square 1536x1536 Meshy image-to-3D source image, a single isolated National Cyber Innovation Centre building. Reference 1 is architecture/material truth: the large meadow wedge on the right, not other campus blocks. Geometry: rectangle 60m long x35m wide, ONE uninterrupted planar sloping wildflower meadow roof from essentially ground level at the near LOW 35m end to 14m/four storeys at the far HIGH 35m end. No flat roof section, no folds, no ridge, no separate blocks. Thin pale buff stone borders follow the entire slope, low end a thin pale stone lip, long sides triangular pale buff stone with horizontal glazing bands under the slope, high end glazed. Natural finely textured green and straw meadow with tiny wildflowers only on roof. Three-quarter view from LOW end/front-left corner, showing low short end, left long side and roof. Camera 28 degrees above horizontal, equal 45 degree azimuth to plan axes, moderate 70mm lens, distant weak perspective, verticals vertical. Entire building centrally framed with at least 12% clear margin on all sides, maximum width about 76% of square. Plain seamless uniform light grey studio floor/background no horizon. Soft even diffuse overcast illumination, subtle contact shadow only, no strong cast shadows or baked-in lighting. NOTHING else: no landscape, trees, people, sky, vehicles, furniture, detached base, text, labels, logos, watermark. Clean realistic materials, neutral unlit glazing. Single image, single building.
