experiments/002-living-map/meshy/src/codex-notes.md:29:Use case: product-mockup. A2 square Meshy source view. Supplied image is the exact building identity to preserve. Orbit camera 180 degrees to opposite BACK-RIGHT/HIGH-END corner: show fully glazed 35m wide 14m tall HIGH end in foreground and the previously hidden opposite triangular 60m long side receding to the ground-level low tip. NOT a mirror image of low-end view. Same exact 60x35x14m single meadow wedge, one continuous planar meadow roof and thin pale stone edges, same buff stone, same horizontal glazing bands with tall glazing near high end on opposite long side. High-end facade curtainwall glazing with four storeys subtle mullion/transom grid, pale stone perimeter. Preserve same camera elevation 28 degrees and distance, focal length, object scale and square canvas as input. Entire building alone visible clear margins all sides. Seamless light grey studio background, soft even diffuse overcast light, only thin contact shadow. No landscape, trees, people, cars, furniture, sky, base, text or watermark. Single image.
