experiments/002-living-map/meshy/src/codex-notes.md:37:Use case: product-mockup. B1: square single isolated architectural building Meshy source view. Reference courtyard supplies exact linear buff-grey fine brick-slip/stone texture, strong horizontal bands, recessed regular windows and pale timber soffit; do not reproduce courtyard or joined wings. One pure rectangular bar 38m LONG x17m DEEP x14m HIGH, exactly FOUR storeys TOTAL: fully glazed 3.5m ground floor and THREE upper floors of recessed regular windows. Crucial physical ratios length/depth=2.2353, length/height=2.7143, depth/height=1.2143. Flat sedum roof with low pale parapet, one small central array of SIX PV panels (two rows of three), no rooftop structures. Front and back long elevations matching regular 12 window bays per upper floor, each short end 5 window bays per upper floor. Neutral grey glazing, dark bronze slim frames. Pale timber soffit above fully glazed ground floor. Camera FRONT-LEFT corner equal 45-degree azimuth to axes, elevation28 degrees, moderate focal length weak perspective verticals upright. Show front 38m facade and left17m end plus roof. The projected long horizontal edge must be 2.235 times short horizontal edge at equal azimuth. Entire building with 10% or greater blank margins. Seamless plain light grey studio background and floor, no horizon. Soft even diffuse overcast daylight, only thin contact shadow, no strong shadows or baked light. No sky, landscaping, people, trees, cars, furniture outside or inside, surrounding blocks, base, labels, text, watermark. One image one building.
