experiments/002-living-map/session-log.md:45:`scripts/golden_valley_slice.py` builds the whole dataset: 2×2 km box (E 390400–392400, N 221400–223400) fetched at native 1 m from both the DTM and the last-return DSM; **DSM − DTM = measured height of everything standing on the ground**. 4,042 OSM footprints rasterised against that difference grid give 4,033 buildings, each extruded to its median measured height (median 5.7 m — two-storey Benhall, correct; the page renders them as an archviz white model over the terrain, no vertical exaggeration).
